# Bitcoin Lifeboat - Meetup Workshop Kit

_A hands-on self-custody class for up to fifteen people._

## 1. Safety warning

Never enter a real seed phrase into a website or this workshop's software. This class uses test wallets only.

Bitcoin Lifeboat never asks for a seed phrase. Teach attendees that anyone who does is a scammer.

## 2. Do not panic

Remind attendees that recovery is a slow, careful process and that this class is a safe place to make and discuss mistakes.

Keep the pace relaxed. Allow time for questions after each step.

## 3. Stop and call a trusted helper

Teach the habit: when a step is unclear, stop and ask. In real recovery the helper is a trusted person; in this class it is the instructor.

Instructor / helper on the day: ______________________

## 4. Required materials checklist

- [ ] Up to 15 printed copies of this kit.

- [ ] A projector or large screen for the live demo.

- [ ] Test (Signet or regtest) descriptors and sample wallet files.

- [ ] A computer per small group with the wallet software in section 10.

- [ ] Spare paper and pens for blank fields.

## 5. Wallet type summary

Run the class with a simple single-signature test wallet first, then a 2-of-3 multisig if time allows.

- Script type used today: wpkh

- Number of keys: 1

## 6. Descriptor backup reminder

Walk attendees through reading a descriptor and explaining each part. Use only test descriptors in class.

Recovery details: [descriptor redacted, see private export]

## 7. Signer/device checklist

For the multisig demo, show how each signer device contributes one signature.

- Demo signer A: short code ________

Demo device location / owner: ______________________

## 8. Passphrase existence reminder

Explain that a passphrase (a 25th word) is optional and, if used, must be stored apart from the seed. Never demonstrate with a real passphrase.

## 9. Emergency contacts

Attendees fill these in for their own real setup after class.

My trusted helper: ______________________

My attorney or executor: ______________________

## 10. Wallet software dependency list

Install these before class so attendees can follow along:

- Sparrow

## 11. Verification steps

1. Load a test descriptor in watch-only mode and read it together.

2. Derive the first address and confirm everyone sees the same one.

3. Sign and broadcast a Signet transaction as a group.

4. Have each attendee write their own next-step plan.

## 12. Stop conditions

Pause the class and reset if:

- Anyone is about to use a real seed phrase or real funds.

- An attendee feels lost; slow down and review.

